# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Other | Scene: TheWarIsWon

translate es strings:

    old "Sarah awakes the next day in her bed. It was already very bright outside; she wondered how long she had slept."
    new "Sarah despierta al día siguiente en su cama. Ya era muy de día afuera; se preguntó cuánto tiempo había dormido."

    old "Memories of the day before come back to her."
    new "Los recuerdos del día anterior regresan a ella."

    old "The battle."
    new "La batalla."

    old "Her and Varga, in the bed..."
    new "Her y Varga, en la cama..."

    old "Sarah recalled Marion and the audacity of his proposal."
    new "Sarah recordó a Marion y la osadía de su propuesta."

    old "Sarah recalled letting her brother, Varga and Marion to themselves. They had earned their celebration."
    new "Sarah recordó dejar a su hermano, Varga y Marion solos. Habían merecido su celebración."

    old "She rubbed her temples, trying to physically drive out the memories and focus on the day."
    new "Frotó sus sienes, tratando de expulsar físicamente los recuerdos y centrarse en el día."

    old "Sarah got out of bed and began to dress herself."
    new "Sarah se levantó de la cama y comenzó a vestirse."

    old "She wondered in what state she would find her brother."
    new "Se preguntaba en qué estado encontraría a su hermano."

    old "After wandering the castle for some time, she followed echoes of muted sounds, the embers of a celebration."
    new "Después de vagar por el castillo durante un tiempo, siguió los ecos de sonidos apagados, las brasas de una celebración."

    old "She came upon Thomas in the great hall, where he sat on the steps up to the throne, a last few soldiers still lingering around."
    new "La encontró a Thomas en la gran sala, donde él se sentaba en los escalones que llevaban al trono, con un par de soldados aún rondando por ahí."

    old "If their behavior hadn't been enough to let Sarah know they were drunk, the smell would have settled it."
    new "Si su comportamiento no había sido suficiente para que Sarah supiera que estaban borrachos, el olor lo habría confirmado."

    old "It surprised her how young many of the soldiers were, barely much older than Thomas. Children really, she thought."
    new "Le sorprendió lo jóvenes que eran muchos de los soldados, apenas un poco mayores que Thomas. Niños realmente, pensó."

    old "As she came closer, she cleared her throat, gathering their attention."
    new "A medida que se acercaba, aclaró la garganta para llamar su atención."

    old "I think the celebrations have come to an end. Time you all got some much-needed rest."
    new "Creo que las celebraciones han terminado. Es hora de que todos descansen un poco."

    old "The soldiers offered up some slurred protest, but most were by now so exhausted they welcomed an excuse to put an end to their partying."
    new "Los soldados lanzaron unas quejas tartamudeadas, pero la mayoría ya estaba tan exhausta que bienvenía cualquier pretexto para poner fin a su fiesta."

    old "Only Thomas remained, still laying across the steps. A bottle of wine dangling in his loose grip."
    new "Solo Thomas permanecía, aún tendido sobre los escalones. Una botella de vino colgando de su agarre flojo."

    old "Enjoying yourself, I see?"
    new "Disfrútalo, ¿eh?"

    old "Thomas chortled."
    new "Thomas carcajeó."

    old "It was quite something, Sis, I'll tell you that."
    new "Era algo bastante impresionante, hermana; te lo digo."

    old "I hadn't even noticed it was already day again."
    new "Ni siquiera noté que ya era de nuevo día."

    old "I think you'd probably do well to get some rest. Your head is going to feel like it's splitting open soon enough."
    new "Creo que harías bien en descansar un poco. Pronto sentirás que tu cabeza se va a partir por la mitad."

    old "Thomas laughed."
    new "Thomas rió."

    old "Or maybe that means I should just carry on, skip all the headache."
    new "O quizás eso significa que debería seguir adelante, saltarme todo el dolor de cabeza."

    old "Sarah crossed her arms."
    new "Sarah se cruzó los brazos."

    old "You might be king, but you're also my little brother, and unlike those sycophants, you can trust me to tell you what you actually need, not just what you want to hear."
    new "Podrías ser rey, pero también eres mi pequeño hermano, y a diferencia de esos aduladores, confío en decirte lo que realmente necesitas, no solo lo que quieres oír."

    old "And you need to rest."
    new "Y necesitas descansar."

    old "Thomas gave a drunkard's nod."
    new "Thomas asintió con la cabeza de un borracho."

    old "You're right, you're right. Just give me a moment."
    new "Tienes razón, tienes razón. Dame solo un momento."

    old "Sarah sat down on the stairs next to Thomas. She put one hand on his shoulder."
    new "Sarah se sentó en los escalones al lado de Thomas. Le puso una mano en el hombro."

    old "You know, Thomas, you were very brave yesterday. But if you ever want to talk to me about that day, I mean, really talk, you know you can right?"
    new "Sabes, Thomas, fuiste muy valiente ayer. Pero si alguna vez quieres hablar conmigo de ese día, quiero decir, hablar de verdad, sabes que puedes hacerlo, ¿verdad?"

    old "Thomas sat up."
    new "Thomas se sentó erguido."

    old "It was incredible, Sarah, absolutely incredible."
    new "¡Fue increíble, Sarah, absolutamente increíble!"

    old "I've never felt anything like it in my life."
    new "Nunca he sentido nada como eso en mi vida."

    old "To meet them in battle, see these people who want nothing more than to kill you, and to fight, knowing your life depends on it."
    new "Conocerlos en batalla, ver a esos hombres que no buscan nada más que matarte y luchar, sabiendo que tu vida depende de ello."

    old "It was exhilarating."
    new "Era exaltante."

    old "Ooh, and when we turned the tide and started to rout them, wow, I can't put it into words."
    new "¡Oh! Y cuando volteamos la marea y comenzamos a aniquilarlos, ¡wow!, no puedo ponerlo en palabras."

    old "Sarah listened to her brother speak. It was clear that he was being honest."
    new "Sarah escuchó a su hermano hablar. Era evidente que era sincero."

    old "She was glad to hear that the battle did not trouble him, but she hadn't expected to see him seemingly enjoying it."
    new "Estaba contenta de escuchar que la batalla no le inquietaba, pero no esperaba verlo disfrutando de ella."

    old "Well, I'm glad to see you're carrying it well, Thomas."
    new "Bien, me alegra ver que lo llevas bien, Thomas."

    old "You're right. I can play tough, and I think I carried myself well, but inside..."
    new "Tienes razón. Puedo ser duro y creo que me porté bien, pero por dentro..."

    old "Sarah...I try to put on this front of the perfect king. Even on the battlefield, I cover up my fears."
    new "Sarah... trato de mantener esta fachada del rey perfecto. Incluso en el campo de batalla, oculto mis miedos."

    old "But all around me, I saw the faces of soldiers, and you could see it in their eyes: they were hungry for the killing."
    new "Pero a mi alrededor, vi las caras de soldados, y se notaba en sus ojos: tenían hambre de matar."

    old "Thomas paused."
    new "Thomas se detuvo."

    old "I'm not sure I can be like that. Not really, you know, on the inside?"
    new "No estoy seguro de poder ser así. No realmente, ¿sabes, por dentro?"

    old "Sarah patted her brother's shoulder to comfort him."
    new "Sarah le acarició el hombro para consolarlo."

    old "I think that's a good thing, Thomas."
    new "Creo que eso es algo bueno, Thomas."

    old "You don't want to be the kind of man that loves bloodshed."
    new "No quieres ser el tipo de hombre que ama la sangre."

    old "War is a necessity, but only when our enemies leave us no other option."
    new "La guerra es una necesidad, pero solo cuando nuestros enemigos no nos dejan otra opción."

    old "Sarah stood up and stuck out her hand to Thomas."
    new "Sarah se puso de pie y extendió la mano hacia Thomas."

    old "Taking his sister's hand, Thomas slowly wobbled his way onto his feet."
    new "Sosteniendo la mano de su hermana, Thomas tambaleó lentamente hasta ponerse de pie."

    old "The bottle slid from his already loose grip and began tumbling down the stairs, rolling off into the hall."
    new "La botella se deslizó de su agarre ya relajado y comenzó a rodar por las escaleras, cayendo al final al pasillo."

    old "Ugh, I really am worse off than I thought."
    new "Vaya, realmente estoy peor de lo que pensaba."

    old "I'll trust you can make it back to your room by yourself, or do I need to get one of the servants to carry you?"
    new "Confío en que puedas volver a tu habitación por ti misma, o ¿necesito enviar a uno de los sirvientes para llevarte?"

    old "Either I'll make it, or you'll find my asleep somewhere in the hallways. Either way, I'll get some rest."
    new "O lograré hacerlo, o me encontrarás durmiendo en algún pasillo. De todos modos, voy a descansar."

    old "Sarah watched her brother stumble away. He had joked, but she was only half sure that she wouldn't actually find him off in some hallway."
    new "Sarah observó a su hermano tambalearse y alejarse. Él había bromeado, pero ella solo tenía la mitad de la certeza de que no lo encontraría de hecho perdido en algún pasillo."

    old "Still, she was glad to find him doing well."
    new "Aun así, estaba contenta de encontrarlo bien."

    old "The battle had taken a lot out of him, but they had pushed out the invaders."
    new "La batalla había exigido mucho de él, pero habían expulsado a los invasores."

    old "Rosanna was safe, for now."
    new "Rosanna estaba segura, por ahora."

    old "Varga was leaning against a wall, reading a map of some sort. His face was very stern when he was focused, and he was too focused to notice Sarah coming upon him."
    new "Varga se apoyaba contra una pared, leyendo un mapa de algún tipo. Su rostro era muy severo cuando estaba concentrado, y tan absorto en ello que no notó el acercamiento de Sarah."

    old "She stuck her hand out, between Varga and the map."
    new "Extendió la mano entre Varga y el mapa."

    old "Startled, his face turned from serious to surprised, only to turn happy when he realized it was Sarah."
    new "Sorprendido, su rostro pasó de la seriedad a la sorpresa, y luego a la alegría al darse cuenta de que era Sarah."

    old "You almost gave me a heart attack."
    new "Casi me das un infarto."

    old "A heart attack? Didn't know you had so many enemies in the castle to be fearful of."
    new "¿Un infarto? No sabía que tuviera tantos enemigos en el castillo de los que tener miedo."

    old "Just one in particular that's always trying to get me in trouble."
    new "Solo uno en particular que siempre intenta meterme en problemas."

    old "Varga looked at her intently."
    new "Varga la miró con atención."

    old "Is that so? Any plans on how you're going to deal with this dangerous enemy?"
    new "¿Es eso así? ¿Tienes algún plan para lidiar con este peligroso enemigo?"

    old "A few."
    new "Unos pocos."

    old "So mysterious."
    new "Tan misteriosa."

    old "Varga folded up his map."
    new "Varga dobló su mapa."

    old "Anything I can help you with, Sarah?"
    new "¿Hay algo en lo que pueda ayudarte, Sarah?"

    old "Sarah shook her head and spun around on the back of her heels."
    new "Sarah sacudió la cabeza y giró sobre los talones."

    old "I was going to take care of some work, but now I've found myself distracted by you."
    new "Iba a ocuparme de algunos asuntos, pero ahora me he encontrado distraída por ti."

    old "Sarah waved her finger at Varga."
    new "Sarah le señaló con el dedo a Varga."

    old "Keeping me from my royal duties, it's treasonous really."
    new "Mantenerme de mis deberes reales es traición, en serio."

    old "Don't let me get in the way, go right ahead. The library is off that way, but I imagine you know your way around the castle."
    new "No te interpongas en mi camino, adelante. La biblioteca está por ahí, pero imagino que conoces los pasillos del castillo."

    old "Sarah sighed."
    new "Sarah suspiró."

    old "Ugh, you're no fun."
    new "¡Joder, no eres divertida!"

    old "Varga chuckled."
    new "Varga carrasqueó con risa."

    old "You seemed to think otherwise last night."
    new "Parecías pensar lo contrario anoche."

    old "Sarah looked around, making sure they were alone."
    new "Sarah miró a su alrededor, asegurándose de que estaban solos."

    old "Maybe that was just clouded judgement from the alcohol."
    new "Quizás solo fuera un juicio nublado por el alcohol."

    old "Varga suddenly grabs Sarah by the waist, spins her around and pins her with her back against the wall."
    new "Varga agarró de repente a Sarah por la cintura, la giró y la clavó con la espalda contra la pared."

    old "He pauses for a moment."
    new "Pausa un momento."

    old "Sarah parts her lips, encouraging him on."
    new "Sarah abre los labios, animándolo a continuar."

    old "Varga leans in, pressing his lips against hers."
    new "Varga se inclina, presionando sus labios contra los suyos."

    old "Sarah feels him pinning her body against the wall as his tongue slides into her mouth."
    new "Sarah siente cómo lo aprisiona contra la pared mientras su lengua se desliza en su boca."

    old "She eagerly meets his with hers."
    new "Ella se une a la suya con ansias."

    old "For a moment his hands explore her body over her dress, but then she finds him suddenly backing off."
    new "Por un momento sus manos exploran su cuerpo por encima del vestido, pero luego ella lo ve retirarse de golpe."

    old "Sarah reaches with her mouth, desperately trying to get him back on her."
    new "Sarah se abalanza con la boca, desesperada por volver a tenerlo entre sus piernas."

    old "She only finds Varga smiling back at her, still holding her up against the wall."
    new "Solo encuentra a Varga sonriéndole, aún sosteniéndola contra la pared."

    old "So, what's your excuse now?"
    new "¿Cuál es tu excusa ahora?"

    old "Sarah knew she had none, nor would she offer any if she had. She wanted him to take her right now if they could get away with it."
    new "Sarah sabía que no tenía nada, ni siquiera lo ofrecería si tuviera algo. Quería que él la tomara ahora mismo, si podían hacerlo sin ser vistos."

    old "But the castle was full of wandering servants, always watching, listening, gossiping."
    new "Pero el castillo estaba lleno de sirvientes errantes, siempre vigilando, escuchando, chismesando."

    old "She felt her unsatisfied lust make way for frustation."
    new "Sintió cómo su lujuria insatisfecha cedió lugar a la frustración."

    old "So proud of yourself."
    new "Tan orgullosa de ti misma."

    old "Sarah pushed Varga aside and stepped back into the middle of the hallway."
    new "Sarah empujó a Varga hacia un lado y dio un paso atrás, colocándose en el centro del pasillo."

    old "You're angry?"
    new "¿Estás enojada?"

    old "I just...I wish we could be together, really together."
    new "Solo... solo deseo que estemos juntos, de verdad."

    old "Varga took her hand."
    new "Varga tomó su mano."

    old "I know, Sarah. But out here...we need to be careful."
    new "Lo sé, Sarah. Pero aquí fuera... tenemos que tener cuidado."

    old "Sarah pulled her hand away and began to walk towards the library."
    new "Sarah retiró la mano y comenzó a caminar hacia la biblioteca."

    old "She mumbled to herself in frustration."
    new "Murmuraba para sí misma con frustración."

    old "Always so damn careful."
    new "Siempre tan cuidadosa, por Dios."

    old "Sarah set out for the library to take care of the day's duties."
    new "Sarah se dirigió a la biblioteca para atender las tareas del día."
